---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"How a Hotel Loan Sale Works"} description={"Six steps from a confidentiality agreement to funds wired, and what the bank and the buyer each provide at every stage of a hotel loan sale."}>
  <Hero eyebrow={"For banks"} title={"How a hotel loan sale works."} lead={"Six steps from a confidentiality agreement to funds wired. What each side provides at each stage."} />
  <SectionNav section="banks" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">The process</p><h2>Six steps from a confidentiality agreement to funds wired.</h2></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Confidentiality agreement</h3><p>We sign yours or provide ours before any loan-level information is shared.</p></li>
        <li><h3>One-page summary</h3><p>Balance, status, the hotel's brand and room count, and any recent valuation. A full file is not needed yet.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Indicative price</h3><p>We respond with a price and the assumptions behind it, or tell you the loan is not for us.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Due diligence</h3><p>We review the loan file, title, franchise documents, and operating results, and inspect the hotel.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Loan sale agreement</h3><p>A purchase agreement with a fixed price and closing date.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Closing</h3><p>Funds are wired, the note is endorsed, the mortgage is assigned, and the file is transferred.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section" id="step-1"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Step 01</p><h2>Confidentiality agreement</h2><p>Nothing about the loan is shared until an agreement is in place.</p></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>On the bank's side</h3><p>Its own form of confidentiality agreement, or acceptance of ours.</p></div>
        <div><h3>On our side</h3><p>Sign the bank's agreement or provide ours. We receive no loan-level information before it is signed.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section alt" id="step-2"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Step 02</p><h2>One-page summary</h2><p>A short description of the loan and the hotel is enough to start. A full file is not needed yet.</p></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>On the bank's side</h3><p>The balance, payment status, the hotel's brand and room count, and any recent valuation. The <a class="more arrow" href="/banks/information-to-send/">full list</a> is short.</p></div>
        <div><h3>On our side</h3><p>Read the summary and decide whether the loan is one we can price.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section" id="step-3"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Step 03</p><h2>Indicative price</h2><p>A price, with the assumptions behind it, or a plain no.</p></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>On the bank's side</h3><p>Nothing at this stage beyond the summary. A conversation and an indicative price carry no obligation to sell.</p></div>
        <div><h3>On our side</h3><p>Respond with a price and the assumptions behind it, or tell you the loan is not for us. If a loan is not for us, the seller hears that within days, with the reason.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section alt" id="step-4"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Step 04</p><h2>Due diligence</h2><p>The work that lets us hold to the figure once we have given it.</p></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>On the bank's side</h3><p>The loan file, title information, franchise documents, and operating results, and access for an inspection of the hotel. We do not contact the borrower, guarantors, the brand, or hotel staff without the bank's consent.</p></div>
        <div><h3>On our side</h3><p>Review the file, title, franchise documents, and operating results, and inspect the hotel. The figure does not move without a reason found in diligence.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section" id="step-5"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Step 05</p><h2>Loan sale agreement</h2><p>A purchase agreement with a fixed price and closing date.</p></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>On the bank's side</h3><p>Review and sign the agreement. Loans are commonly sold <a href="/glossary/#as-is">as-is and without recourse</a>, with the bank giving limited representations, such as that it owns the loan and has authority to sell it. The terms are negotiated, and the price and closing date are fixed in the agreement.</p></div>
        <div><h3>On our side</h3><p>Agree the terms and sign. We provide proof of funds, and we do not rely on third-party financing to close.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section alt" id="step-6"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Step 06</p><h2>Closing</h2><p>The loan, the file, and the workout transfer, and the bank is paid.</p></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>On the bank's side</h3><p>The original note with its endorsement or <a href="/glossary/#allonge">allonge</a>, the <a href="/glossary/#assignment-of-mortgage">assignment of mortgage</a>, and the loan file. The bank's involvement ends on the date it chose.</p></div>
        <div><h3>On our side</h3><p>Wire the funds. After closing we contact the borrower directly, with notice of the transfer and where payments go.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="feature"><div class="wrap">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">What stays the same</p><h2>The loan does not change. The holder does.</h2></div>
      <div><p class="lead">When a loan is sold, the loan documents stay the same. The borrower's obligations and rights are the ones already in the note, mortgage, and any guaranty. What changes is who makes the decisions.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-light arrow" href="/borrowers/">What owners should expect</a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/library/checklist/">Hotel loan diligence checklist <span>Library</span></a></li><li><a href="/blog/why-special-servicers-sell-hotel-notes/">Why special servicers sell hotel notes, and what bidders are expected to bring <span>Blog</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#note-sale">Note sale (loan sale) <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/underwriting/">What we examine before we price a hotel loan <span>Underwriting</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Discuss a hotel loan in confidence."} text={"A conversation and an indicative price carry no obligation to sell."} label={"Start a conversation"} />
</Base>
